    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! All tests are passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n## Summary of Changes\n\nI fixed two issues in the frai-core test suite:\n\n1. **eval/metrics.js**: Updated the `toxicityMetric` function signature from `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)` to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms)`. This makes it consistent with other metrics (`exactMatchMetric`, `lengthVarianceMetric`) which accept both outputs and references. The `runEvaluations` function calls all metrics with the same signature `metric(outs, refs)`, so the toxicity metric was receiving references as banned terms, causing incorrect scoring.\n\n2. **finetune/index.js**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `DEFAULT_GOVERNANCE_TEMPLATE`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS`. The test was importing `APPROVAL_STATUSES` directly from `./index.js`, but it wasn't being re-exported at the module level.\n\nAll 28 frai-core tests and 11 frai-gate tests now pass, with all public exports preserved.",
